{"result":"{
  "id": "18477",
  "key": "SFCC-247",
  "summary": "Spike: Validate Magento Product Hierarchy Against SFCC Variation Model",
  "description": "\\*\\*Objective\\*\\*\nUsing the Magento sample product extract (SFCC-29), investigate whether Zimmermann's existing product hierarchy in Magento maps cleanly to the SFCC master → variation group → variant model, and document any gaps or transformations required before SFCC-25 (Product Type and Variation Model) is configured.\nDocumentation here on Confluence: [Product Hierarchy - Adobe SFCC - Confluence](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/247234568/ProductHierarchy)\n\\*\\*Background\\*\\*\nSFCC uses a strict three-level product hierarchy:\n- \\*\\*Master product\\* — shared attributes (name, style code, description); not purchasable\n- \\*\\*Variation group\\* — groups variants by colour; holds colour-level attributes and images\n- \\*\\*Variant (SKU)\\* — purchasable unit; unique colour  size combination with its own price and inventory\nBefore configuring this model in BM (SFCC-25), we need to confirm that Magento's product structure can be mapped to it — or identify where custom transformation logic will be needed.\n\\*\\*Tasks\\*\\*\n- Extract and review a representative sample of products from Magento (see SFCC-29)\n- Map Magento product attributes to the SFCC three-level hierarchy\n- Identify any structural mismatches (e.g. flat product structure, missing colour/size grouping, non-standard variant logic)\n- Document any transformation or custom logic required to fit Magento data into the SFCC model\n- Flag any attributes present in Magento that have no equivalent in the SFCC attribute schema (SFCC-26)\n\\*\\*Definition of Done\\*\\*\nA documented mapping (or gap analysis) is produced and reviewed, confirming whether SFCC-25 can proceed as-is or whether the story needs updating before configuration begins.",
