{"result":"{
  "id": "18581",
  "key": "SFCC-297",
  "summary": "PDP UI — Find in Boutique Button and Slide-In Panel",
  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "1. Given a product is eligible for Find in Boutique, when the shopper lands on the PDP, then a Find in Boutique button/CTA is displayed.\n2. Given the shopper clicks Find in Boutique, when the modal opens, then it displays the product image, name, colour and price at the top.\n3. Given the modal is open, when no size has been selected, then a size selector dropdown is shown with a prompt to select a size.\n4. Given the shopper selects a size in the modal, when boutique results are returned, then each boutique is listed with its name, address, open/closed status, distance, and one of three availability states: Available / Low Stock / Out of Stock.\n5. Given a boutique row is collapsed, when the shopper clicks Explore Boutique, then it expands to show opening hours, phone number, email, Google Maps embed, and a Get Directions link.\n6. Given a boutique row is expanded, when the shopper clicks to collapse it, then the boutique details are hidden.\n7. Given the shopper clicks Get Directions for a boutique, when clicked, then Google Maps opens in a new tab with the route pre-populated to that boutique's address.\n8. Given the shopper clicks Use Location, when geolocation permission is granted, then the store locator field is populated with their current location and results are sorted by proximity.\n9. Given the shopper types a country, city, state or street into the location search field, when they submit, then boutique results are filtered and sorted by proximity to that location.\n10. Given no boutiques have the selected size in stock, when results are displayed, then a clear empty state message is shown.\n11. Given the modal is open on mobile, when rendered, then the modal displays in a full-width slide-up panel consistent with Zimmermann mobile design patterns.\n12. Given the shopper clicks the close (X) icon, when clicked, then the modal closes and the shopper is returned to the PDP."
  }
}"}

